{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`--key=value` flags are now split on the first `=` instead of being stored as a boolean named `key=value`.\n\n`parse_flags` treated everything after `--` as the flag name. For `--out=log.txt` that produced `{\"out=log.txt\": True}`. When the argument contains `=`, the parser now splits once: the left side is the name and the right side is the value, so `--out=log.txt` becomes `{\"out\": \"log.txt\"}`. Extra `=` characters stay in the value.\n\nThe other forms are unchanged: `--out log.txt` still reads the next argument, and a bare `--flag` is still `True`."}]},"session_id":"8fb0e77f-e025-4067-a142-6a1cea990491"}
